{"id":"6530ee2fa245fe46","group":"73","path":"73/73-thm-binary-many-one-transitivity.md","title":"Transitivity of Computable Many-One Reduction","display":"thm-many-one-reduction-transitive — Transitivity of Computable Many-One Reduction","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Automata Theory, Languages and Computation (Hopcroft, Ullman)","book_abbrev":"73","label":"73-thm-binary-many-one-transitivity","aliases":["73-thm-binary-many-one-transitivity","73-thm-many-one-reduction-transitive"],"display":"thm-many-one-reduction-transitive — Transitivity of Computable Many-One Reduction","depends_on":["[[73-df-binary-many-one-reduction]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Automata Theory, Languages and Computation (Hopcroft, Ullman)"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"73"},{"key":"label","html":"73-thm-binary-many-one-transitivity"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>73-thm-binary-many-one-transitivity</span><span>73-thm-many-one-reduction-transitive</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-many-one-reduction-transitive — Transitivity of Computable Many-One Reduction"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"64d902370bb28edb\" href=\"?note=64d902370bb28edb\" title=\"73-df-binary-many-one-reduction\">73-df-binary-many-one-reduction</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\leq_m\">\\(\\leq_m\\)</span> (computable many-one reducibility on binary languages, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"64d902370bb28edb\" href=\"?note=64d902370bb28edb\" title=\"73-df-binary-many-one-reduction\">73-df-binary-many-one-reduction</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}many\\text{-}one\\text{-}reduction\\text{-}transitive}\\vdash\n\\forall A,B,C\\subseteq\\mathbf 2^*\\;\n\\bigl(A\\leq_m B\\land B\\leq_m C\\longrightarrow A\\leq_m C\\bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}many\\text{-}one\\text{-}reduction\\text{-}transitive}\\vdash\n\\forall A,B,C\\subseteq\\mathbf 2^*\\;\n\\bigl(A\\leq_m B\\land B\\leq_m C\\longrightarrow A\\leq_m C\\bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>If total computable functions <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"f\">\\(f\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"g\">\\(g\\)</span> witness the two premises, then <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"g\\circ f\">\\(g\\circ f\\)</span> is total computable and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"x\\in A\\leftrightarrow f(x)\\in B\\leftrightarrow g(f(x))\\in C\">\\(x\\in A\\leftrightarrow f(x)\\in B\\leftrightarrow g(f(x))\\in C\\)</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"73-df-binary-many-one-reduction","status":"resolved","id":"64d902370bb28edb","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[73-df-binary-many-one-reduction]]","embed":false},{"target":"73-df-binary-many-one-reduction","status":"resolved","id":"64d902370bb28edb","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\leq_m$ (computable many-one reducibility on binary languages, see [[73-df-binary-many-one-reduction]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"\\leq_m","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}many\\text{-}one\\text{-}reduction\\text{-}transitive}\\vdash\n\\forall A,B,C\\subseteq\\mathbf 2^*\\;\n\\bigl(A\\leq_m B\\land B\\leq_m C\\longrightarrow A\\leq_m C\\bigr)","display":true},{"tex":"f","display":false},{"tex